SUMMARY:Improv 201 With Scott!
DESCRIPTION:Learned the Basics? Let's Learn How to do a Show! About the Cla
 ss: Welcome to Lancaster Improv Players' 201 class! This 8-week long cours
 e focuses on the more advanced skills of long-form Improv. Students will l
 earn skills which include game of a scene\, second beats\, heightening\, a
 nd advanced character work. This class focuses on teaching a ton of scene 
 work skills and will help improvisers think beyond the scene they are in. 
 The class ends with a graduation show where the students can show their fr
 iends and family the skills learned. This class does require Improv 101 as
  a prerequisite or director approval. Class Schedule: This class runs for 
 two and a half (2.5) hours for eight (8) sessions on Mondays from 7pm-9:30
 pm. Those dates are 10/19\, 10/26\, 11/2\, 11/9\, 11/16\, 11/23\, 11/30\, 
 and 12/7. The Class Show is on Saturday 12/12 at 4pm! Important: Please ch
 eck your email the week prior to the start date of your class for any upda
 tes. To qualify for the class show you must: Adhere to the Lancaster Impro
 v Players' Code of Conduct. Attend at least six of the eight sessions (ide
 ally all eight). Attend at least two improv shows during the length of the
  class. During the class you receive standby tickets for all of our regula
 r shows. These tickets get you into shows for free so long as the show has
  not soldout! Tickets are on sale until end of day Friday 10/16!\n\nPrice:
